---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/layout/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/layout/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout>
  <slot name="head">
    <title>How Our Video to Image Converter Works - Step-by-Step Guide</title>
    <meta name="description" content="Learn how our video to image converter works in three simple steps: upload video, choose extraction method, download frames. Discover how to convert video to JPG, PNG, and other formats client-side.">
    <meta property="og:title" content="How Our Video to Image Converter Works - Step-by-Step Guide">
    <meta property="og:description" content="Learn how our video to image converter works in three simple steps: upload video, choose extraction method, download frames. Discover how to convert video to JPG, PNG, and other formats client-side.">
    <meta property="og:image" content="/logo.svg">
    <meta property="og:url" content="https://freevideotoimage.com/how-it-works">
    <meta property="og:type" content="website">
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image">
    <meta name="twitter:title" content="How Our Video to Image Converter Works - Step-by-Step Guide">
    <meta name="twitter:description" content="Learn how our video to image converter works in three simple steps: upload video, choose extraction method, download frames. Discover how to convert video to JPG, PNG, and other formats client-side.">
  </slot>
  <Header currentPath="/how-it-works" />
  <main class="flex-1">
    <!-- Hero Section -->
    <section class="relative">
      <div class="relative z-10 pt-20 pb-16 md:pt-28 md:pb-20">
        <div class="container">
          <div class="text-center">
            <h1 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3 text-center">How It Works</h1>
            <p class="body-lg max-w-[600px] mx-auto text-center">
              Simple workflow, powerful results. Extract frames in three easy steps.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <!-- Mesh Gradient Background -->
      <div class="absolute inset-0 -z-0 pointer-events-none">
        <svg width="100%" height="100%" viewBox="0 0 100 100" preserveAspectRatio="none">
          <defs>
            <linearGradient id="gradient" x1="0%" y1="0%" x2="100%" y2="100%">
              <stop offset="0%" stop-color="{colors.cyan}" />
              <stop offset="25%" stop-color="{colors.violet}" />
              <stop offset="50%" stop-color="{colors.pink}" />
              <stop offset="75%" stop-color="{colors.magenta}" />
              <stop offset="100%" stop-color="{colors.cyan}" />
            </linearGradient>
          </defs>
          <rect width="100" height="100" fill="url(#gradient)" opacity="0.08" />
        </svg>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- How It Works Section -->
    <section class="pt-16 md:pt-20 pb-12">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="text-center mb-16">
          <span class="mono-eyebrow mb-3">Step-by-Step Guide</span>
          <h2 class="heading-lg mb-4 text-center">How to Extract Frames from Video</h2>
          <p class="body-md max-w-[500px] mx-auto text-center">
            Follow these simple steps to extract frames from any video using our client-side tool.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 xl:grid-cols-2">
          <!-- Step 1: Upload -->
          <article class="feature-card hover:shadow-[0px_2px_8px_rgba(0,0,0,0.04)] transition-shadow">
            <div class="relative">
              <div class="absolute -top-4 left-6 bg-[var(--color-ink)] text-[var(--color-on-primary)] text-3xl font-bold w-12 h-12 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center">
                1
              </div>
              <div class="pt-8">
                <h3 class="heading-md mb-3">Upload Your Video</h3>
                <p class="body-md">
                  Click the upload area or drag & drop your video file. Supported formats include MP4, WebM, MOV, AVI, and more. Maximum file size is 2GB.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </article>

          <!-- Step 2: Choose Extraction Mode -->
          <article class="feature-card hover:shadow-[0px_2px_8px_rgba(0,0,0,0.04)] transition-shadow">
            <div class="relative">
              <div class="absolute -top-4 left-6 bg-[var(--color-ink)] text-[var(--color-on-primary)] text-3xl font-bold w-12 h-12 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center">
                2
              </div>
              <div class="pt-8">
                <h3 class="heading-md mb-3">Select Extraction Method</h3>
                <p class="body-md">
                  Choose from three extraction modes: Manual Capture (frame-by-frame), Interval Extraction (automatic at set intervals), or Smart Scene Detection (key moments only).
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </article>

          <!-- Step 3: Adjust Settings -->
          <article class="feature-card hover:shadow-[0px_2px_8px_rgba(0,0,0,0.04)] transition-shadow">
            <div class="relative">
              <div class="absolute -top-4 left-6 bg-[var(--color-ink)] text-[var(--color-on-primary)] text-3xl font-bold w-12 h-12 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center">
                3
              </div>
              <div class="pt-8">
                <h3 class="heading-md mb-3">Configure Settings</h3>
                <p class="body-md">
                  Adjust extraction parameters like interval time, scene sensitivity, output format (PNG/JPG/WebP/AVIF), and quality level to match your needs.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </article>

          <!-- Step 4: Extract -->
          <article class="feature-card hover:shadow-[0px_2px_8px_rgba(0,0,0,0.04)] transition-shadow">
            <div class="relative">
              <div class="absolute -top-4 left-6 bg-[var(--color-ink)] text-[var(--color-on-primary)] text-3xl font-bold w-12 h-12 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center">
                4
              </div>
              <div class="pt-8">
                <h3 class="heading-md mb-3">Extract Frames</h3>
                <p class="body-md">
                  Click the extract button to begin processing. The tool works entirely in your browser - no data leaves your computer.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </article>

          <!-- Step 5: Review -->
          <article class="feature-card hover:shadow-[0px_2px_8px_rgba(0,0,0,0.04)] transition-shadow">
            <div class="relative">
              <div class="absolute -top-4 left-6 bg-[var(--color-ink)] text-[var(--color-on-primary)] text-3xl font-bold w-12 h-12 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center">
                5
              </div>
              <div class="pt-8">
                <h3 class="heading-md mb-3">Preview & Select</h3>
                <p class="body-md">
                  Review extracted frames in the gallery. Use checkboxes to select specific frames for download, or choose all frames.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </article>

          <!-- Step 6: Download -->
          <article class="feature-card hover:shadow-[0px_2px_8px_rgba(0,0,0,0.04)] transition-shadow">
            <div class="relative">
              <div class="absolute -top-4 left-6 bg-[var(--color-ink)] text-[var(--color-on-primary)] text-3xl font-bold w-12 h-12 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center">
                6
              </div>
              <div class="pt-8">
                <h3 class="heading-md mb-3">Download Your Frames</h3>
                <p class="body-md">
                  Download selected frames individually or as a ZIP archive. All processing is client-side ensuring complete privacy.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Detailed Tutorial -->
    <section class="pt-12 md:pt-16 pb-10 bg-[var(--color-canvas-elevated)]">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="text-center mb-12">
          <span class="mono-eyebrow mb-3">Detailed Tutorial</span>
          <h2 class="heading-lg mb-4 text-center">Step-by-Step Instructions</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="prose lg:prose-lg mx-auto">
          <h3 class="heading-md mb-4">Getting Started</h3>
          <p>
            Begin by navigating to the <a href="/video-to-image-converter" class="text-[var(--color-primary)] hover:underline">Video to Image Converter</a>
            tool. The interface is divided into three main sections: Upload, Extraction Controls, and Results Gallery.
          </p>

          <h3 class="heading-md mb-4">Step 1: Upload Your Video</h3>
          <p>
            Click the large upload area or drag and drop your video file onto it. The tool supports all major video formats
            including MP4, WebM, MOV, AVI, MKV, and more. Maximum file size is 2GB. Once uploaded, you'll see video information
            including duration, resolution, and file size displayed below the upload area.
          </p>

          <h3 class="heading-md mb-4">Step 2: Choose Your Extraction Method</h3>
          <p>
            Select one of three extraction modes based on your needs:
          </p>
          <ol class="list-decimal list-inside space-y-2">
            <li><strong>Manual Capture:</strong> Ideal when you need exact control over which frames to extract. Use the frame-accurate
                scrubber to navigate to specific moments and click "Capture Frame" to save each one.</li>
            <li><strong>Interval Extraction:</strong> Perfect for creating timelapses or extracting frames at regular intervals.
                Set the interval time (e.g., every 5 seconds) and define start/end times if you only want to process a portion of the video.</li>
            <li><strong>Smart Scene Detection:</strong> Best for extracting only key moments when the scene changes significantly.
                Adjust the sensitivity threshold to control what qualifies as a scene change.</li>
          </ol>

          <h3 class="heading-md mb-4">Step 3: Configure Output Settings</h3>
          <p>
            Before extracting, choose your preferred output format and quality:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2">
            <li><strong>PNG:</strong> Lossless format ideal for editing, design work, and archival purposes</li>
            <li><strong>JPG:</strong> Adjustable quality from 70-95% - perfect for web use and sharing where file size matters</li>
            <li><strong>WebP:</strong> Modern format offering superior compression with good quality - great for web applications</li>
            <li><strong>AVIF:</strong> Next-generation format with the best compression ratios (available in Safari 16.4+ and Chrome)</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            For JPG, WebP, and AVIF formats, you can adjust the quality slider to balance between file size and image quality.
          </p>

          <h3 class="heading-md mb-4">Step 4: Extract Your Frames</h3>
          <p>
            Click the "Extract Frames" button to begin processing. Depending on your video length and selected method,
            extraction may take a few moments. The progress indicator will show you how far along the process is.
            Importantly, all processing happens in your browser - your video never leaves your computer.
          </p>

          <h3 class="heading-md mb-4">Step 5: Review and Select Frames</h3>
          <p>
            Once extraction completes, you'll see all extracted frames in the gallery below. Each frame shows:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2">
            <li>The timestamp showing where in the video the frame was captured</li>
            <li>A checkbox to select/deselect the frame for download</li>
            <li>A download icon to save that individual frame immediately</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Use the "Select All" or "Deselect All" buttons to quickly choose which frames you want to download.
            Selected frames are highlighted with a blue ring.
          </p>

          <h3 class="heading-md mb-4">Step 6: Download Your Results</h3>
          <p>
            When you've selected the frames you want to save, you have two download options:
          </p>
          <ol class="list-decimal list-inside space-y-2">
            <li><strong>Download Selected:</strong> Saves only the frames you've checked as a ZIP archive</li>
            <li><strong>Download All as ZIP:</strong> Saves every extracted frame in a single ZIP file</li>
          </ol>
          <p>
            For large extractions, the tool uses streaming download to handle the transfer efficiently without
            consuming excessive memory. All downloads happen immediately and are saved to your default download folder.
          </p>

          <h3 class="heading-md mb-4">Tips for Best Results</h3>
          <p>
            <strong>For precise frame selection:</strong> Use Manual Capture mode and the arrow keys for frame-by-frame navigation</p>
          <p>
            <strong>For timelapse creation:</strong> Use Interval Extraction with intervals matching your desired playback speed</p>
          <p>
            <strong>For highlighting key moments:</strong> Use Smart Scene Detection and adjust sensitivity until you get the desired number of frames</p>
          <p>
            <strong>For editing workflows:</strong> Choose PNG format for lossless quality that won't degrade through multiple edits</p>
          <p>
            <strong>For web sharing:</strong> Choose JPG at 85% quality or WebP for excellent compression with good visual quality</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>